## 2. What the Red test file holds

tests/preset-colour.test.ts has four tests.

1. The recolour formula on a saturated default. Slot default #d9443a, options #f2c230, #e8892c,
   #4f9a4a, #7b4a9e, #3f6fa8, #f4f1ea. A texel equal to the default must become the option
   within 3/255. Result: PASS.
2. The same slot with k.tint shade -0.25. The recoloured shade must equal the option shade within
   6/255. Result: PASS.
3. The baked preset atlases. It runs scripts/preset-colour-check.mjs on ball, kite, paint-splash,
   and paint-pot and expects exit 0. Result: FAIL (exit 1). This is the Red.
4. The pin. Every asset under assets/*.ts that declares variants and presets must keep its pinned
   ratio, recoloured default, and recoloured -0.25 shade within 1/255. Result: PASS. The test
   compares 387 assets, 902 presets, and 3166 preset slots. The allow-list INTENDED_CHANGES is
   empty. Green fills it only with entries the fix must move, each with a reason.

So the formula is not the cause. Tests 1 and 2 pass at HEAD. Test 4 passes because the pin records
today's code. Test 3 fails because the baked texels of ball and kite drift.

