## 5. Root cause: the texels, not the formula

- The formula residual is 0 or 1 of 255 on every eligible texel of all four assets. The code of
  src/variants.ts recolor reproduces the baked preset atlas exactly. The formula is correct.
- The ball has zero anchor texels in every slot and every preset. The whole leather surface is
  lifted by `k.tint(slot, 0.03 + 0.05 * sheen)` in assets/ball.ts. The stored default texel is
  therefore not the slot default. The mean default is #db5e58, not #d9443a. The default preset
  (redyellow) already drifts by 29.6/255. A lighter texel multiplied by a saturation ratio gives
  gold. Red to orange has ratios (1.16, 4.33, 0.60). The stored lit red (linear 0.711, 0.108,
  0.093) becomes (0.827, 0.467, 0.055), about #e9b642. That is the gold in N1. The measured
  orangewhite panel A mean is #eab944 against the option #e8892c.
- The kite lifts its upper sail by `k.tint(slot, 0.10)` in assets/kite.ts. The lift is a mix
  toward white in linear light, so it adds blue to yellow and green to red. The ratio then
  amplifies the lift. Yellow to red has a blue ratio of 1.43; the lit yellow becomes rose. Red to
  yellow has a green ratio of 9.33; the lit red becomes lemon. The anchor set holds only the
  mid-sail texels that are exactly the default, so the check catches sailA/yellow (15/255) and
  not sailB/red (7/255). The sailB/red mean error is 15.7/255; the lit quarter is the rose part.
- Test 1 and test 2 pass because an exact default and a -0.25 shade follow the contract. A -0.25
  shade is a multiply, so it is safe. A positive shade is an add toward white, so it is not.
- paint-pot is clean: every texel is the exact default (anchors 24977 of 24977, error 0). Its
  paint colour is not lifted.
- The mask is stored as an sRGB byte of the linear coverage (src/asset.ts composeAtlas), and
  recolor reads the byte as linear coverage. This overweights soft-mask texels. It is not the
  cause of N1 or N2: those texels are fully masked (mask 250 to 255) and the residual is 0 or 1.
  Green should keep it in view, but the 11 failing slots do not need it.

A fix on the formula cannot keep tests 1 and 2 green and remove this drift. The visible cause is
the positive shade baked into the base atlas. Green either removes the positive shade from the
ball and kite (and rebuilds the textures), or changes the bake so a positive shade does not add
white to the stored slot texel. A change to the formula would also move the pin, which is empty
today.

